    "lawCode": "Amd §1229-c, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A8612A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to requiring\nchildren under the age of 8 to be restrained by a child restraint system\nin a motor vehicle\n\nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\nThis bill would enhance highway safety for children who are passengers\nin motor vehicles.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 of the bill would amend Vehicle and Traffic Law (\"VTL\")\n1229-c(1)(b) to increase, to age 7, the maximum age at which children\nover the age of four are required to be restrained in booster seats\nwhile they are passengers in the back seat of an automobile.\n\nSection 2 of the bill would make the same amendment to VTL,\n1229-c(2)(c), regarding front seat passengers.\n\nSections 3 and 4 of the bill would make conforming amendments to VTL\n1229-c(6) and (12), respectively, concerning the increased maximum age\nof child passengers subject to the booster seat requirement.\n\nSection 5 of the bill would provide that the bill would take effect 90\ndays after it becomes law.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\nCurrently, the VTL requires only children ages four through six to be\nrestrained in child passenger restraint systems.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nA.11083-A passed the Assembly in 2007.\n\nSTATEMENT IN SUPPORT:\nPursuant to two recent enactments (Chapter 509 of the Laws of 2004 and\nChapter 18 of the Laws of 2005), ages four through six are required to\nbe restrained in special booster seats, as are those under four who\nweigh more than forty pounds. However, according to the Center for\nDisease Control growth charts, while 95% of children under the age of\neight weigh less than 80 pounds. All current booster seats are certified\nfor at least 80 pounds and many, up to 100 pounds. The average eight\nyear old is about 50\" tall (4 feet 2 inches) and 96% of this age group\nare under 54\" (4 feet 6 inches). Due to the difference in anatomy\nbetween adults and children, the recommended height to use an adult seat\nbelt is 4 feet 9 inches. Therefore, including 7 year olds in the booster\nseat requirement is a reasonable step that recognizes the reality of the\nphysical size of this age group, and will enhance the safety of these\nchildren when they are passengers in an automobile.\n\nBUDGET IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill would take effect 90 days after receiving Executive approval.\n\n",
